WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.714
<v Nina Kowalski>Okay, I looked at the pricing, it's reasonable and I want to move forward on the SMB plan.</v>

00:00:08.414 --> 00:00:16.557
<v Jordan Ruiz>Great, I'll get the agreement sent to you today. For billing, do you want monthly card billing or invoicing?</v>

00:00:17.257 --> 00:00:29.257
<v Nina Kowalski>Card billing is easier for us. Let me just give you the number now so we don't have to deal with another step — it's 4111 1111 1111—</v>

00:00:29.957 --> 00:00:52.243
<v Jordan Ruiz>Nina, actually let me stop you there — I'm not able to take card numbers directly over the phone, both for your security and ours. I'll send you a secure billing portal link where you can enter it directly and it never passes through me or gets logged in our call system.</v>

00:00:52.943 --> 00:00:56.371
<v Nina Kowalski>Oh, sure, that makes sense, sorry about that.</v>

00:00:57.071 --> 00:01:06.500
<v Jordan Ruiz>No problem at all, happens more than you'd think. I'll send that link along with the contract in the next few minutes.</v>

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.771
<v Nina Kowalski>Sounds good. Once that's done, how fast can we get started on setup?</v>

00:01:13.471 --> 00:01:27.186
<v Jordan Ruiz>As soon as the contract's signed and the portal is completed, I'll hand you off to onboarding same day — given your three-week timeline, we'll prioritize getting your EDI connector live first.</v>

00:01:27.886 --> 00:01:31.314
<v Nina Kowalski>Perfect, that's exactly what I need to hear.</v>

00:01:32.014 --> 00:01:42.729
<v Jordan Ruiz>I'll also confirm your best contact number on file in case billing or onboarding ever needs to reach you quickly — is (775) 555-0122 good?</v>

00:01:43.429 --> 00:01:46.000
<v Nina Kowalski>Yes, that's my cell, that's best.</v>

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.129
<v Jordan Ruiz>Great, sending everything over now. Welcome to Cascadence.</v>
